1.13.0: grain belongs to the film - speed and granularity per stock

Grain was the last camera/film fusion: every stock through a camera
got identical texture. Amount now scales ~sqrt(ISO) parsed from the
film stem against the camera's canonical stock (defaults render
unchanged), texture by a gentler fourth root, with grain-family
modifiers: tabular (T-Max, Delta, Acros, XP2) finer, color dye clouds
softer, HIE grittier; trailing +/- stem tokens count as push stops, so
the measured push variants earn their grain. Implemented centrally in
the engine; CLI, superjuice, wasm and page all pass the stem (wasi
render grows a FILMSTEM arg). Core tests assert the speed ladder
orders variance (Pan F < HP5 < Delta 3200) and tabular runs finer than
cubic at equal speed (T-Max < Tri-X); no stem means no change.
